 "standard_url": "https://www.education.gov.za/Portals/0/CD/National%20Curriculum%20Statements%20and%20Vocational/CAPS%20FET%20_%20MATHEMATICS%20_%20GR%2010-12%20_%20Web_1133.pdf",
 "standard_text": "An intuitive understanding of the concept of a limit; differentiation of specified functions from first principles: f′(x) = lim<sub>h→0</sub> [f(x + h) − f(x)]/h.",
 "meta_desc": "Free CAPS Grade 12 calculus worksheets: limits, f(x + h) − f(x) and derivatives from first principles. 100 questions with memos.",
 "key_big": "f′(x) = lim (f(x + h) − f(x)) ÷ h.",
 "key_sub": "0 ÷ 0: factorise first.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>For a polynomial, find a limit by substituting.</li><li>If substituting gives <span class='fr'><span class='fn'>0</span><span class='fd'>0</span></span>, factorise and cancel first.</li><li>First principles: f′(x) = lim<sub>h→0</sub> <span class='fr'><span class='fn'>f(x + h) − f(x)</span><span class='fd'>h</span></span>.</li><li>Expand, simplify, divide by h, then let h → 0.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>f(x) = 2x²</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>f(x + h) − f(x) = 4xh + 2h²</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>÷ h: 4x + 2h</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: f′(x) = 4x</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>0 ÷ 0</td><td>It is not 0: factorise first.</td></tr><tr><td>Missing terms</td><td>Expand every bracket.</td></tr><tr><td>The sign</td><td>The derivative of a/x is −a/x².</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What does CAPS Grade 12 say?",
   "a": "Understand intuitively the concept of a limit, and differentiate specified functions from first principles."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is h?",
   "a": "A small change in x."
  },
  {
   "q": "Why let h → 0?",
   "a": "The secant becomes the tangent."
  },
  {
   "q": "What does f′(x) mean?",
   "a": "The gradient of the tangent at x."
  }
 ],
